--------------------------------
          Comparing
        C++ Libraries
--------------------------------
This column compares two class libraries:

(1) Rogue Wave's "tool.h" library, derived
    from the NIH class library which was
    the standard 3-4 years ago.
(2) Code Farms' library, the new standard
    needed for today's advanced projects.

Example:

Assume the following data organization

          ............................
          :     C o m p a n y        :
          :..........................:
           1      1              1
           |      |              |
    byDate |      | byRev        | depts
           |      |              |
           n      n              n
  ....................       ..........................
  :  P R O J E C T   :       :  D E P A R T M E N T   :
  :..................:       :........................:
              1                  1
              |                  |
              | byProj           | byDept
              |                  |
              n                  n
          ............................
          :     E m p l o y e e      :
          :..........................:

The two libraries implement this data differently.
For 5 projects, 5 departments, and 8 employees, 
they need:                     
                               
      Rogue W: 50 objects,114 pointers 
      Code F:  19 objects, 69 pointers

Rogue Wave classes follow the old Smalltalk style,
while Code Farms library uses a natural C++ design
style which leaves classes independent for modular
testing.

